# Python Port Plan — Step 04: The API Client

## Goal

Port `week1_baseline/ruby/04_api_client` to
`week1_baseline/python/04_api_client`. This step adds a `Client` class that
takes a `PromptBuilder`, sends one real HTTP POST to the configured LLM
provider (with retry/backoff on transient errors and retryable status
codes), and returns the parsed JSON response — no tool-call handling yet,
that's step 5. Also adds an `ApiError` exception and two small robustness
fixes to `Tasks::Base`. Same behavior, same example output shape, same
shared `.boukensha/` fixture directory as the Ruby version.

**⚠️ Safety note carried into execution**: `example.rb`'s Python port will
make a real network call to the configured provider (Anthropic, per the
current `.boukensha/settings.yaml`) using the real API key in `.env`. Running
it costs a small amount of real API credits. Flag this before running the
ported example, the way the Ruby original already does implicitly.

