  failure path (e.g. temporarily using a bad API key to trigger a 401,
  which should raise `ApiError` with the expected message shape) to confirm
  `Client`'s error handling works, without needing to fake a transient
  network error.
- `week1_baseline/python/04_api_client/README.md` documents `Client`'s
  retry/backoff behavior, the `PROMPTS_DIR` bug fix, the `requests`-library
  dependency deviation, and the real-network-call caveat.
